    2. Choose 4 distinct colors — bg, left_fg, right_fg, separator — with bg=BLACK, others from non-BLACK palette [observed].
    3. Generate left binary mask — fill H x W panel with bg, randomly set 40-60% of cells to left_fg.
    4. Generate right binary mask — fill H x W panel with bg, randomly set 40-60% of cells to right_fg.
    5. Ensure at least 1 cell where both are fg (overlap) and at least 1 cell where exactly one is fg (non-trivial XOR output).
    6. Concatenate left_panel, separator column, right_panel to form input grid.
    7. Output = XOR mask — bg where both agree, RED where exactly one has fg.
